<h2><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"></span></strong></span><strong>1️⃣</strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">A bit of history</span></strong></span></h2>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span></p>

<ul>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>13 September 1954:</strong></em> The draft statutes of the new company, named “Lignes aériennes intérieures (Air Inter)”, are filed with the registry of the Seine commercial court.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>12 November 1954:</strong></em> Official creation of Air Inter Lignes Aériennes Intérieures.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>16 March 1958:</strong></em> Air Inter Lignes Aériennes Intérieures, better known under its commercial name Air Inter, operates its first commercial flight on the Strasbourg–Paris route with a Douglas DC-3 flight ITF011. Operations also begin with chartered aircraft: Douglas DC-3, DC-4, Super DC-6B, Vickers Viking and Lockheed Constellation.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>21 July 1958:</strong></em> Start of operations of the chartered Sud-Est SE 3130 Alouette II, operating connections between Orly and Le Bourget.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>01 April 1962:</strong></em> First commercial flight of the Vickers Viscount.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>21 July 1964:</strong></em> Entry into service of the Nord 262B Frégate.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>24 February 1967:</strong></em> Air Inter becomes independent with the entry into service of the Caravelle III, which replaces the Viscount.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>03 August 1968:</strong></em> Delivery of the Fokker F27-500 after evaluation of the Fokker F27-300. It succeeds the Nord 262B Frégate.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>19 October 1972:</strong></em> Arrival of the Caravelle 12 in the fleet.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>16 May 1974:</strong></em> Entry into service of the first Dassault Mercure 100.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>20 January 1977:</strong></em> Start of operations of the Airbus A300 (first in B2-1C version, then in B4-2C version).</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>March 1988:</strong></em> Trial of the Boeing 747-128A on the Paris Orly–Marseille and Paris Orly–Toulouse routes.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>17 June 1988:</strong></em> Delivery of the first Airbus A320-111.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>30 December 1993:</strong></em> Delivery of the first Airbus A330-301.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>05 March 1995:</strong></em> Entry into service of the first Fokker F28-0100 (Fokker 100).</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>31 December 1995:</strong></em> Last Air Inter flight on the Ajaccio–Paris Orly route, flight ITF5046.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>01 January 1996:</strong></em> Start of operations of Air France Europe under the commercial name Air Inter Europe.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>21 June 1996:</strong></em> Entry into service of the first Airbus A319.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>11 March 1997:</strong></em> Transfer of the last Airbus A319 (and last Air Inter Europe aircraft) to Air France.</span></li>
	<li data-end=\"2202\" data-start=\"165\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><em><strong>01 April 1997:</strong></em> Official disappearance of Air Inter.</span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"></span></p>

<p data-end=\"2422\" data-start=\"2204\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Air Inter therefore existed for 43 years, including 39 years of commercial operations. The two years of operations preceding the closure of Air Inter were carried out on behalf of Air France in Air Inter Europe livery.</span></p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"></span></p>

<p data-end=\"2677\" data-start=\"2424\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Air Inter was the largest European regional airline, a French pride. It also operated the Dassault Mercure 100, another French pride. A magnificent aircraft far ahead of its time, which could largely have dethroned its direct competitor, the Boeing 737.</span><br />
<br />
&nbsp;</p>

<h2><strong>2️⃣</strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"><strong>Your career</strong></span></span><br />
&nbsp;</h2>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Building on this historical information, Air Inter Virtual Airlines offers you the opportunity to organize your career over three periods of Air Inter’s life, taking you back in time to discover older aircraft and a different way of flying, where glass cockpits and FMCs do not exist. You will also have the possibility to continue your career within a subsidiary and a division: Inter Cargo Service (a direct subsidiary of Air Inter) and Air Charter International (a division of Air France and Air Inter).<br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"><strong>a) 1st period 1982-1997</strong></span></span><br />
<br />
We begin the journey back in time. This most recent period corresponds to the beginning of your career at Air Inter Virtual Airlines but also marks the end of Air Inter. It will satisfy the greatest number of you. The aircraft listed below were actually used by Air Inter during this period and will therefore be offered to you for company flights:</span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Sud Aviation Caravelle Super&nbsp;12</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Dassault Mercure 100</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A300-B4-2C</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 747-123 LX-LCV (</span>leased from<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Cargolux between 01/04/1987&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;29/10/1987,&nbsp;</span>used on<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Paris, Marseille, Nice, Toulouse and Bordeaux)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 747-123 LX-MCV (</span>leased from <span style=\"color:#000000;\">Cargolux&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">between</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;01/07/1986&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;02/07/1986,&nbsp;</span>used on<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Paris, Marseille, Nice, Toulouse and Bordeaux)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 747-128A F-BPVD (</span>leased from <span style=\"color:#000000;\">Air France&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">between</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;01/04/1988&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;30/04/1989,&nbsp;</span>used on<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Paris, Marseille, Nice, Toulouse and Bordeaux)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 747-2B4B N204AE (</span>leased from <span style=\"color:#000000;\">Nigeria Airways&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">between</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;11/11/1986&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;30/06/1987,&nbsp;</span>used on<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Paris, Marseille, Nice, Toulouse and Bordeaux)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Fokker F28-0100 (better known as Fokker 100)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A319-113 (under Air Inter Europe livery)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A320-111 (first version of the&nbsp;A320 without winglet)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A320-211 (most well-known version with&nbsp;winglets)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A321-111</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A330-301</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<br />
<span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"><strong>b) 2nd period 1970-1981</strong></span></span><br />
<br />
We go a little further back in time. This is the Air Inter period when glass cockpits were still unknown and when “flying an airplane” was still truly “flying an airplane”, but not for much longer… Here is the list of aircraft that were actually used by Air Inter at that time and that will be offered to you once you are admitted to this period:</span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Fokker F27-500</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Vickers Viscount 708</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Vickers Viscount 724</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Sud Aviation Caravelle III</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Sud Aviation Caravelle VI-R (leased from Catair from December 1975 and December 1979)</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Dassault Mercure 100</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A300-B2-1C</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A300-B4-2C</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Douglas DC-8-63PF (</span>leased from<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">UTA between 01/04/1974 and 31/10/1975&nbsp;</span>while awaiting delivery of the <span style=\"color:#000000;\">Dassault Mercure 100)</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<br />
<span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"><strong>c) 3rd period 1958-1969</strong></span></span><br />
<br />
We continue our journey back in time to reach the beginning of the great Air Inter adventure, which also marks the beginning of the end of the golden age of aviation. A time when ILS was very little widespread and when flying a QDM variation approach required very great mental “gymnastics”, while piloting an aircraft almost completely devoid of automation (something that almost all current pilots would be quite incapable of doing, myself included). Once again, the aircraft listed below were actually used by Air Inter at that time and will be offered to you once you are admitted to this period:</span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Douglas DC-3 (non-pressurized, leased from Air France)</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Vickers Viking VC-1 (</span>non-pressurized, leased from Airnautic<span style=\"color:#000000;\">)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Douglas DC-4 (</span>(non-pressurized, leased from Aéromaritime, UAT<span style=\"color:#000000;\">)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Douglas Super DC-6B (</span>leased from&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\">Transports Aériens Intercontinentaux, TAI</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Lockheed L-749A Constellation (</span>with and without speedpack, leased from Air France<span style=\"color:#000000;\">)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Lockheed L-1049G Super Constellation (</span>leased from <span style=\"color:#000000;\">Air France)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Vickers Viscount 708</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Nord N260A Super Bushranger</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Nord N262B Frégate</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Fokker F27-500</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">SE 3130 Alouette II</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">d) The Inter Cargo Service subsidiary</span></strong><br />
<span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"></span></span><br />
Inter Cargo Service was the direct subsidiary of Air Inter, created in 1987 to meet the growing demand for air cargo transport. Inter Cargo carried passengers by day and freight by night. The company was renamed “Inter Ciel Service” in 1990 and then “Aéropostale” in 1991. The aircraft used by the subsidiary are:</span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Lockheed L-100-30 Hercules all-cargo.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Vickers Vanguard 953C all-cargo.</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 737-2Q2C Quick Change passenger/cargo.</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">e) The Air Charter International division</span></strong></span><br />
<br />
Air Charter International was a division of Air France and Air Inter, created in 1966 under the name SAFA – Société Aérienne Française d’Affrètement, then renamed Air Charter International in 1970. Flights operated by Air Charter International are carried out on behalf of Air France, Air Inter, Euralair and Europe Aero Service. With the merger of Air France and Air Inter, the company ceased to have a purpose and closed in 1998. The aircraft used by this division are:</span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Lockheed L-1049G Super Constellation (leased from Air France)</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Fokker F28-4000 (better known as Fokker 28 and&nbsp;</span>leased from<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;Touraine Air Transport, TAT)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Sud-Aviation SE-210 Caravelle III</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Sud-Aviation SE-210 Caravelle 10B3</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Dassault Mercure 100 (</span>leased from<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Air Inter)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 727-214 ADV</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 737-222</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 737-400</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 737-500</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 747-200 (</span>leased from<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Air France)</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A300-B4-203</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A310-324</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Airbus A320-212</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Any other aircraft at the discretion of the members.</span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\"></span></strong></span></p>

<h2><strong>3️⃣</strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">Progression through the 3 periods, the subsidiary and the division</span></strong></span></h2>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span></p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Minimum required hours to progress through the different periods and access the 2 subsidiaries:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span>Newly hired pilot: The newly hired pilot is on probation for the first&nbsp;10 flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Flight Engineer: 10 flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">First Officer: 100</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Captain: 200</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Instructor : 500</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span><br />
	&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The only requirement is to complete at least 1 flight every 60 days.<br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span></span><br />
<span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Once you reach the rank of Captain, you will gain access to the subsidiaries Intercargo Services and Air Charter International.<br data-end=\"130\" data-start=\"127\" />
Flight hours and PIREPs will be credited within these subsidiaries, but not within Air Inter itself.</span><br />
<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span><br />
<strong>Air Inter Virtual Airlines wishes you a long and successful career…</strong></span></p>
